    <h3>Reading the numbers</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>AUCP growth has decelerated.</strong> YoY AUCP revenue growth ran 770% (2020→21), 113% (2022), 22% (2023), 16% (2024), and 7% (2025). This mirrors the underlying sales plateau — fixed-fee revenue (license, registration) grows with operator count, while excise-pools-volume grows with sales.</li>
      <li><strong>Medical sales tax to GF declined.</strong> $15.06M (FY2024) → $14.28M (FY2025), a 5.2% YoY decline. Counter-intuitive given patient-certification growth, but consistent with caregiver-channel sales still going tax-exempt on the caregiver-to-patient transfer.</li>
      <li><strong>January 1, 2026 reset.</strong> The biennial budget (P.L. 2025, ch. 388) restructured these effective Jan 1, 2026 — see the next section for the line-by-line changes.</li>
    </ul>
